# Sim and coordinates

World: +X east, +Y **south** (Ebiten Y-down). Lot **640×1280**. Origin NW. Spawn `(320, 1180)`, heading `0` = north.

```go
// heading 0 → north (0, -1); heading increases clockwise
func Forward(heading float64) (fx, fy float64) {
    return math.Sin(heading), -math.Cos(heading)
}
```

`A` = vehicle **left** (heading decreases). At south-facing that is screen-right. That is correct tank-steer — do not “fix” it to screen-absolute left. Reverse is first-class. Camera is world-fixed north and **does not yaw**.

Physics uses continuous `heading`. `FacingIndex` is draw-only.

## Solidity

Dozer body is a circle (`DozerBodyR`). Buildings, rubble, blockers are AABBs. Resolve with `CircleAABB` (max 3 iterations). No physics engine. No tile-grid collision.

Buildings have three states: Intact → Cracked → `InRubble`. Rubble is real collision. **Never delete rubble** — it is the maze.

## Heat, plates, threats

Heat and plates are sprite state (palette / vents), not HUD numbers. Cooked engine or `Plates == 0` → same tally as the buzzer.

Cruisers peel **side/rear** only when blade is **up** and `CruiserPIT`. Frontal blade-down kills the cruiser. Excavator boom peels any stance. Chopper never peels and is not deletable.

Boons live as flags on `run.Run` (sheriff → no PIT, yard → dumps gone / walls brittle, plant → concrete never sets). Beat chart fires **once** from `Run.Time()` (`Tick/60 + PressureBonus`).

Simulation order is `stepPlay` in `sim.go` (impl guide §8). Follow it; do not invent a second clock.
